The solution would involve explaining how to use Jekyll's templating system to iterate through posts and collect specific front matter variables (in this case, the "animal" attribute). This can be done with Liquid templates in Jekyll, and the solution would be something like:

```liquid
<ul>
{% for post in site.posts %}
  {% if post.animal %}
    <li>{{ post.animal }}</li>
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</ul>
```

